# Pairs with StrictIsolation. Weakening the gate from "the registry says
# committed" to "the registry has not said aborted" is the read-uncommitted
# default: a saga still in flight surfaces its prepared writes to readers.
MODULE: StrictIsolationInflightSurfaces
TARGET: StrictIsolation
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: surfaces a prepared bucket unless the saga has aborted, so in-flight writes are readable

--- FIND
SurfaceViaGate(t, k) == RegistryView(t) = "committed" /\ ~AlreadyTerminal(t, k)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the gate now admits anything not yet known to have aborted, which
\* includes "inflight". This is the strict-isolation default inverted: absence
\* of a decision reads as permission rather than as refusal.
SurfaceViaGate(t, k) == RegistryView(t) # "aborted" /\ ~AlreadyTerminal(t, k)
--- END
